    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an email-uniqueness rule to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline so that creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by another owner is rejected with **409 Conflict**, matching the existing duplicate-telephone pattern.\n\nNew files:\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (like `DuplicateTelephoneException`).\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 409 with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`.\n- `rest/function/owner/CheckUniqueOwnerEmail.java` \u2014 the pipeline step. Reads the normalized email from the published `OwnerFieldsDto`; email is optional so a null/blank email is never a conflict; otherwise scans existing owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` on a case-insensitive match.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 maps the exception to its handler.\n\nWiring:\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `checkUniqueEmail` step (governed by `transaction`) between `normalizeEmail` and `checkUnique`, so the check runs on the already-lower-cased email and before `build`/`save`, meaning no owner is created on conflict.\n\nThe email comparison lower-cases both sides defensively, though `NormalizeOwnerEmail` already lower-cases the incoming email upstream. Both the target test (`coreRejectsDuplicateEmail`) and the full suite are green.",
